## Summary
A research team at Sahmyook University, led by Professor Lee Yong-woo, has scientifically validated the effectiveness of Virtual Reality (VR) in physical therapy education. The study provides empirical evidence supporting VR as an innovative tool to enhance therapeutic training methods. This advancement contributes to improving educational outcomes in healthcare fields.

## Key Points
- Scientific proof of VR's effectiveness in physical therapy education
- Research conducted by Sahmyook University's team under Professor Lee Yong-woo
- Potential to revolutionize training approaches for physical therapists


